  teach:'1) Show the card: "This is a solo — one player, one spotlight."\n2) The step-back: the band does not leave — it steps BACK and lowers to a hush, so the soloist floats on top. Hear it in any song: the sudden quiet around the solo.\n3) The short truth: a solo can be EIGHT BEATS — a little shine is a real solo. Long is not the point; brave is.\n4) The kind quiet: when the room goes quiet for a solo, that is ATTENTION, not judgement — the audience is leaning in.\n5) Play the spotlight game below and close: "one player, all ears."',
  say:'"A solo is the spotlight moment — the band steps BACK, the room goes quiet, and one player carries it! And here are the secrets: a solo can be just EIGHT BEATS — short and shining is a real solo. The quiet audience is on your side — that silence is them leaning in. Play your eight beats, take your bow, and the band comes roaring back!"',
