  childSay:'Your child might say: "One player in the spotlight!" "Eight shining beats!" or the soloist: "The quiet was them leaning in — I played my solo!"',
  real:'Solos lift out of every song: the guitar break, the drum fill, the a-cappella verse — listen for the step-back tonight and name the solo when it arrives. Eight beats of shine, everywhere.',
  play:'The Spotlight: the family band plays a steady groove (pot, shaker, hum) — then the leader\u2019s hand rises: the band steps to a hush, and the SOLOIST of the round plays eight shining beats alone — any instrument, any sounds. Hand falls: the band ROARS back. Every player gets a solo, every solo gets the full applause, every soloist bows. One player, all ears — courage, in eight-beat servings.',
  tips:'Eight beats, exactly — the limit is what makes it brave instead of scary. And the band\u2019s ROAR back is essential: the solo always ends in reunion, which is why children ask to solo again.',
